  {
    "udt_struct_v0": {
      "doc": "Sub-invocation pre-authorized for the target of a `RouteStep`. `arg_refs`\\nmaps `auth_arg_idx \\xe2\\x86\\x92 resolved-step-arg_idx`, threading runtime values\\nfrom prior returns into the declaration so the SAC's byte-exact auth-args\\ncheck (and u128\\xe2\\x86\\x94i128 coercion) match the actual sub-call.\\n\\nAuth semantics (deliberate, known trade-off): declarations are flattened \\xe2\\x80\\x94\\neach entry is emitted as a top-level sibling with no `sub_invocations`, so\\nnested auth trees are not expressible and the host consumes entries by\\nexact `(contract, fn_name, args)` match with no ordering or call-stack\\nposition guarantee. An entry intended for a deep sub-call can therefore be\\nconsumed from any position in the callee's call tree. Exposure is bounded:\\nentries are re-issued per step and live only for that step's invocation,\\neach authorizes exactly one byte-exact action, and routes are constructed\\nby the Rango backend against vetted callee contracts.",
      "lib": "",
      "name": "AuthDeclaration",
      "fields": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "arg_refs",
          "type_": {
            "map": {
              "key_type": "u32",
              "value_type": "u32"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "args",
